<div class=Section1>

<p><span style='font-size:10.0pt;font-family:Verdana'>Charter<br>
The Lost Cabal is about freedom but with this freedom <span class=GramE>comes</span>
great responsibility. <o:p></o:p></span></p>

<h3>Rules of Conduct</h3>
<p><span style='font-size:10.0pt;font-family:Verdana'>We only have a few rules
within the guild but we will remain strict with them. We hope that as a member
of the guild, you will uphold them and live by them. <o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p><span style='font-size:10.0pt;font-family:Verdana'>1.) We treat Guild members with respect.<o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p><span style='font-size:10.0pt;font-family:Verdana'>2.) We respect the rights (and camps) of other players. <o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p><span style='font-size:10.0pt;font-family:Verdana'>3.) We remember that there is a person behind the player, and feelings matter.<o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p><span style='font-size:10.0pt;font-family:Verdana'>4.) Disagreements are handled in tells and not over public or guild chat. When arbitration is needed, an officer will be involved.<o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p><span style='font-size:10.0pt;font-family:Verdana'>5.) We help each other when we can, but it is not an expectation.<o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p><span style='font-size:10.0pt;font-family:Verdana'>6.) We set an example of how we would like others to conduct themselves.<o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p><span style='font-size:10.0pt;font-family:Verdana'>7.) We appreciate diversity, including different ways of doing things, and different opinions.<o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p><span style='font-size:10.0pt;font-family:Verdana'>8.) We are here to have fun with friends.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span style='font-size:10.0pt;font-family:Verdana'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>

<span style='font-size:10.0pt;font-family:Verdana;mso-fareast-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-ansi-language:EN-US;mso-fareast-language:
EN-US;mso-bidi-language:AR-SA'><br clear=all style='page-break-before:always'>
</span>

<p><span style='font-size:10.0pt;font-family:Verdana'>New Member Rules<br>
<span class=GramE>Currently</span>, our requirements for guild membership is
simple at the moment. Guild members have to sponsor new applicants into the
guild. Currently, all officers have the power to guild a member. Any new member
though is still considered to be a probationary member for a minimum of 2 weeks
and a maximum of 1 month. <o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p><span style='font-size:10.0pt;font-family:Verdana'>During this time, the
applicant’s performance, behavior and conduct will be observed and noted. After
this period, any member that passes the requirements is considered to be a full
time member of the guild. <o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p><span style='font-size:10.0pt;font-family:Verdana'>Secondary characters are
automatically initiated into the guild once a player has become a full member
of the guild. Members may contact any officer for assistance in this. <o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p><span style='font-size:10.0pt;font-family:Verdana'>For more information on
our guild, feel free to send any one of us a tell in-game. If you are
interested in joining our guild, contact any of the members and request for
them to sponsor you. We look forward to seeing you in Norrath! <o:p></o:p></span></p>

<span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-fareast-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-ansi-language:EN-US;mso-fareast-language:EN-US;
mso-bidi-language:AR-SA'><br clear=all style='page-break-before:always'>
</span>

