     font-family:Verdana'>Two Chancellors will be designated &quot;Vote
     Takers&quot;. One for &quot;Yae&quot; and one for &quot;Nay&quot;. When a
     vote is requested, members will send <span class=GramE>a tell</span> to
     the appropriate Chancellor to indicate their decision. Each of these
     Chancellors will tally the votes they recieved and give the total to the
     Minister of Gatherings who will inform the member body of the outcome.
     Under no circumstances will anyone but these two Chancellors let anyone
     else (including leaders) know who voted which way.<o:p></o:p></span></li>
 <li class=MsoNormal style='mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;
     mso-list:l0 level1 lfo2;tab-stops:list .5in'><span style='font-size:10.0pt;
     font-family:Verdana'>One Chancellor will log the meeting and take notes on
     hot issues, improvements to the agenda, etc.<o:p></o:p></span></li>
</ul>

<p style='margin:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt'><span style='font-size:10.0pt;
font-family:Verdana'>Purely internal issues (ie should we have the next meeting
in the arena instead of east commons) will be passed or vetoed by a simple
majority.<br>
External issues (ie new idea for public relations) will be passed or vetoed by
a 2/3 majority.<br>
Votes to make probationary members into full members will be passed or vetoed
by a 2/3 majority. *Probationary members will have 3 chances to be voted into
full member status if a 2/3 majority is not reached. If a 2/3 majority is not
reached the probationary member will remain as such until the next meeting and
vote.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p style='margin:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt'><span style='font-size:10.0pt;
font-family:Verdana'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>

<span style='font-size:10.0pt;font-family:Verdana;mso-fareast-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-ansi-language:EN-US;mso-fareast-language:
