</span>-->

<p style='margin:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt'><b><u><span style='font-size:10.0pt;
font-family:Verdana'>The Guild Vault<o:p></o:p></span></u></b></p>

<p style='margin:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt'><b><u><span style='font-size:10.0pt;
font-family:Verdana'><o:p><span style='text-decoration:none'>&nbsp;</span></o:p></span></u></b></p>

<p style='margin:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt'><span style='font-size:10.0pt;
font-family:Verdana'>The Guild Vault, overseen by the Ministry of the Treasury,
will be the repository of collective guild wealth and acquisitions. Members may
make donations to the guild vault in the form of items or money.</span></p><!-- In so doing,
they will accrue Vault Points (hereafter referred to as VPs) to spend on
items/money in the vault.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p style='margin:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt'><span style='font-size:10.0pt;
font-family:Verdana'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>

<p style='margin:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt'><span style='font-size:10.0pt;
font-family:Verdana'>Items will be given a value in VPs based on the following
criteria:<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p style='margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-left:.5in;
margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-indent:-.25in;mso-list:l3 level1 lfo3;tab-stops:
list .5in'><![if !supportLists]><span style='font-size:10.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:
12.0pt;font-family:Symbol;mso-fareast-font-family:Symbol;mso-bidi-font-family:
Symbol'><span style='mso-list:Ignore'>·<span style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
</span></span></span><![endif]><span style='font-size:10.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:
12.0pt;font-family:Verdana'>1 VP per AC<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p style='margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-left:.5in;
margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-indent:-.25in;mso-list:l3 level1 lfo3;tab-stops:
list .5in'><![if !supportLists]><span style='font-size:10.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:
12.0pt;font-family:Symbol;mso-fareast-font-family:Symbol;mso-bidi-font-family:
Symbol'><span style='mso-list:Ignore'>·<span style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
</span></span></span><![endif]><span style='font-size:10.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:
12.0pt;font-family:Verdana'>2 VPs per stat raise (str, int, wis, etc)<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p style='margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-left:.5in;
margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-indent:-.25in;mso-list:l3 level1 lfo3;tab-stops:
list .5in'><![if !supportLists]><span style='font-size:10.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:
12.0pt;font-family:Symbol;mso-fareast-font-family:Symbol;mso-bidi-font-family:
Symbol'><span style='mso-list:Ignore'>·<span style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
</span></span></span><![endif]><span style='font-size:10.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:
12.0pt;font-family:Verdana'>1 VP per 10 points of mana/hp raised (ie +20 mana
would equal 2 VPs)<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p style='margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-left:.5in;
margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-indent:-.25in;mso-list:l3 level1 lfo3;tab-stops:
list .5in'><![if !supportLists]><span style='font-size:10.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:
12.0pt;font-family:Symbol;mso-fareast-font-family:Symbol;mso-bidi-font-family:
Symbol'><span style='mso-list:Ignore'>·<span style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
</span></span></span><![endif]><span style='font-size:10.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:
12.0pt;font-family:Verdana'>1 VP per 3 points of save raises (ie +6 vs cold
would equal 2 VPs)<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p style='margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-left:.5in;
margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-indent:-.25in;mso-list:l3 level1 lfo3;tab-stops:
list .5in'><![if !supportLists]><span style='font-size:10.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:
12.0pt;font-family:Symbol;mso-fareast-font-family:Symbol;mso-bidi-font-family:
Symbol'><span style='mso-list:Ignore'>·<span style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
</span></span></span><![endif]><span style='font-size:10.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:
12.0pt;font-family:Verdana'>VPs for weapons will be on the following formula:
damage/delay x 10 + proc value. Proc value will be based on the type of proc.
Damage procs will be worth 1 VP per 10 points of proc, rounded up. Snare/Slow
procs will be 5 VPs per level of the spell effect (ie a 10<sup>th</sup> level
necro spell as a proc would be worth 50 VPs).<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p style='margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-left:.5in;
margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-indent:-.25in;mso-list:l3 level1 lfo3;tab-stops:
list .5in'><![if !supportLists]><span style='font-size:10.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:
12.0pt;font-family:Symbol;mso-fareast-font-family:Symbol;mso-bidi-font-family:
Symbol'><span style='mso-list:Ignore'>·<span style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
</span></span></span><![endif]><span style='font-size:10.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:
12.0pt;font-family:Verdana'>Rarity Modifiers: VP value for an item will be
adjusted based on the rarity or difficulty to obtain of the item. This will be
on a scale from 1 (ultra common) to 50 (ultra rare) and multiply the VP value
of the object.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p style='margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-left:.5in;
margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-indent:-.25in;mso-list:l3 level1 lfo3;tab-stops:
list .5in'><![if !supportLists]><span style='font-size:10.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:
12.0pt;font-family:Symbol;mso-fareast-font-family:Symbol;mso-bidi-font-family:
Symbol'><span style='mso-list:Ignore'>·<span style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
</span></span></span><![endif]><span style='font-size:10.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:
12.0pt;font-family:Verdana'>Cash donations will be worth 1 VP per PP donated.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p style='margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-left:.5in;
margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-indent:-.25in;mso-list:l3 level1 lfo3;tab-stops:
list .5in'><![if !supportLists]><span style='font-size:10.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:
12.0pt;font-family:Symbol;mso-fareast-font-family:Symbol;mso-bidi-font-family:
Symbol'><span style='mso-list:Ignore'>·<span style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
</span></span></span><![endif]><span style='font-size:10.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:
12.0pt;font-family:Verdana'>Negative Values count as 0 VPs<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p style='margin:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt'><span style='font-size:10.0pt;
mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;font-family:Verdana'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>

<p style='margin:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt'><span style='font-size:10.0pt;
mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;font-family:Verdana'>Items may be “purchased” from
the Vault based on the point system defined above.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p><span style='font-size:10.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;font-family:Verdana'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>

<p><span style='font-size:10.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;font-family:Verdana'>In
addition, the Vault will only accept a limited number of any one item, loosely
set at 5. (ie if the vault already contains 5 ulthork hide bracers, they will
not accept a 6<sup>th</sup>.)<o:p></o:p></span></p>
-->
<p><span style='font-size:10.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;font-family:Verdana'>
To remove items from the vault, a donation must be made by those removing the items. These donations can be 
in the form of the items that are being upgraded, any items the withdrawer desires, or an amount of 
money not to exceed what the withdrawer can comfortably afford.
<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p><span style='font-size:10.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;font-family:Verdana'>Loans:<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p><span style='font-size:10.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;font-family:Verdana'>Members
may receive loans from the Vault. Each request will be reviewed and considered
impartially.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p><span style='font-size:10.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;font-family:Verdana'>Tradeskill
Sponsorship:<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p><span style='font-size:10.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;font-family:Verdana'>A
member who has worked their skill in a trade to 51 or higher and is a member of
the Crafters in the Heart division may apply for tradeskill sponsorship. This
would be a grant from the Vault to help them raise their skill.<br clear=all
style='page-break-before:always'>
<!--</span><b><u><span style='font-size:10.0pt;font-family:Verdana'>Raid Loot<o:p></o:p></span></u></b></p>

<p><span style='font-size:10.0pt;font-family:Verdana'>Players can accrue Loot
Points (hereafter referred to as LPs) by attending guild events such as raids,
aid stations, Corpse Extractions, etc. <o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p><span style='font-size:10.0pt;font-family:Verdana'>Raid loot will be
distributed on a &quot;need before greed&quot; basis.<br>
If an item drops that two raid attendees can use, and it's better than what
they have, whichever has the most points will get the item.<br>
If they have the same number of points they will roll out of 101, highest
roller wins.<br>
Guests will be given 50% of their host’s (whoever invited them) LPs to enter
the raid with.<br>
Once an item is recieved in a raid, the LP value of that item is deducted from
the total of the recipient.<br>
Regardless of LPs, each member will receive one item during a raid unless all
people that can use an item that drops have received one.<br>
LPs for attending a raid will be awarded AFTER the raid is completed.<br>
LPs will be halved if the member leaves the raid before the 2/3 duration point
of the raid (ie they leave 1 hour 45 minutes after the beginning of a 3 hour
raid).<br>
Commonly dropped items will be rolled on by all those who can use it and will
not count against the LP total (ie charged wands).<br>
Cash looted during raids will be used to reimburse casters for reagents used
during the raid (ie 20p per peridot for clerics, 175p per coffin for necros,
etc).<br>
Remaining cash loot will be added to the guild vault. <o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p><span style='font-size:10.0pt;font-family:Verdana'>LPs will be awarded for
being an active and participating member in the guild. The following events
have the corresponding LP value:<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<ul type=disc>
 <li class=MsoNormal style='mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;
     mso-list:l1 level1 lfo4;tab-stops:list .5in'><span style='font-size:10.0pt;
     font-family:Verdana'>Attending a non-raid guild event: 15 LPs<o:p></o:p></span></li>
 <li class=MsoNormal style='mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;
     mso-list:l1 level1 lfo4;tab-stops:list .5in'><span style='font-size:10.0pt;
     font-family:Verdana'>Attending a raid guild event: 10 LPs<o:p></o:p></span></li>
 <li class=MsoNormal style='mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;
     mso-list:l1 level1 lfo4;tab-stops:list .5in'><span style='font-size:10.0pt;
     font-family:Verdana'>Corpse Extractions: 5-10 LPs depending on the
     difficulty.<o:p></o:p></span></li>
 <li class=MsoNormal style='mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;
     mso-list:l1 level1 lfo4;tab-stops:list .5in'><span style='font-size:10.0pt;
     font-family:Verdana'>Outstanding Service Award (to be awarded at the time
     of the Service rendered): 1-10 LPs depending on the magnitude of the
     service. (ie saving a dozen lowbies from a rampaging SG while travelling
     through Oasis will be worth about 7 LPs will saving a newbie from 3
     rampaging orc pawns would be worth 3 LPs).<o:p></o:p></span></li>
</ul>

<p style='margin:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt'><span style='font-size:10.0pt;
mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;font-family:Verdana'>Items that can be used by only
one person attending the raid, and the item is better than what they have, the
item will be given to that person and will not count against their
items-per-raid or their LPs.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p style='margin:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt'><span style='font-size:10.0pt;
mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;font-family:Verdana'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>

<p style='margin:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt'><span style='font-size:10.0pt;
mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;font-family:Verdana'>Raids to get a specific person a
specific item will be handled differently. The item in question will
automatically go to the person the raid is for and will not count against their
LPs but may be counted as their item-per-raid.<br clear=all style='page-break-before:
always'>
<b><u>Rewards<o:p></o:p></u></b></span></p>

<p style='margin:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt'><span style='font-size:10.0pt;
mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;font-family:Verdana'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>

<p style='margin:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt'><span style='font-size:10.0pt;
mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;font-family:Verdana'>Rewards will be given to
Cabalists who best exemplify The Lost Cabal spirit at the bi-weekly meetings.
These rewards will be given for outstanding and self-less service to the Guild
or the community at large, but not for those who only perform service in order
to be rewarded.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p style='margin:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt'><span style='font-size:10.0pt;
mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;font-family:Verdana'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>

<p style='margin:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt'><span style='font-size:10.0pt;
mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;font-family:Verdana'>For example:<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p style='margin:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt'><span style='font-size:10.0pt;
mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;font-family:Verdana'><span style='mso-tab-count:1'>          </span>A
member who decides to sit at the docks in Oasis and buff newbies, announcing to
the guild they are doing so, is most likely only doing it for the reward and
will not receive one.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p style='margin:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt'><span style='font-size:10.0pt;
mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;font-family:Verdana'><span style='mso-tab-count:1'>          </span>A
non-member sending a tell to an officer or leader commending so-and-so for
derailing that nasty spectre train that was chewing up lowbies along the beach,
while so-and-so was just passing through, would be grounds for a reward.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p style='margin:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt'><span style='font-size:10.0pt;
mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;font-family:Verdana'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>

<p style='margin:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt'><span style='font-size:10.0pt;
mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;font-family:Verdana'><span style='mso-tab-count:1'>          </span>A
member porting for donations would not be rendering a self-less service and
would not be rewarded.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p style='margin:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt'><span style='font-size:10.0pt;
mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;font-family:Verdana'><span style='mso-tab-count:1'>          </span>A
